refused: d341_plain_plus_on_a_secret.cy:6:26, line 6 column 26
 6 |     let $a: u32.secret = $key + 1;
   |                          ^^^^^^^^
 what: a plain `+` on a secret checks for overflow, which is a branch
 why:  on a secret, maths is written `plus.wrap` or `plus.saturate`, which never branch, since crashing on overflow would tell an attacker one bit about the secret (D341)
